# graph-hooks: unity — Unity's generated folders and project files. Appended by setup-graph-hooks
# when the repo is a Unity project (ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt plus Assets/).
#
# A committed Unity repo with a Unity .gitignore needs none of this: code-review-graph reads only
# `git ls-files`, and graphify merges .gitignore. It matters before the first commit, when
# code-review-graph finds nothing tracked and walks the whole tree (Library/PackageCache holds
# thousands of package .cs files), and on a repo whose .gitignore lacks the Unity rules.
#
# Anchored, so Assets/Build/ and Assets/Plugins/Logs/ stay indexed. Spelled out per case rather than
# as `/[Ll]ibrary/`: code-review-graph compares directory patterns segment by segment as literal
# strings, so a bracket class never matches there.
/Library/
/library/
/Temp/
/temp/
/Obj/
/obj/
/Build/
/build/
/Builds/
/builds/
/Logs/
/logs/
/UserSettings/
/usersettings/
*.csproj
*.sln
*.slnx
